extends ../layouts/main.pug

block vars
  - var title = "The Claw Revolution | Portfolio Blog"
  - var baseUrl = "../"

block nav_links
  a.transition(href=baseUrl + "index.html" class="hover:text-brand-black") Home
  a.transition(href="index.html" class="hover:text-brand-black") Journal

block content
  main.max-w-3xl.mx-auto.px-6.py-24
    article
      .text-xs.font-semibold.tracking-widest.text-brand-gray.mb-6.uppercase Security // 2026.04.15
      h1.text-4xl.font-semibold.hero-title.text-brand-black.mb-12(class="md:text-6xl")
        | The Claw Revolution: Reshaping Web 
        span.editorial-italic.font-normal Security.
      
      p Security in the modern web era is no longer about perimeter defense. It's about distributed resilience. The "Claw" model represents a paradigm shift where every node in a network acts as an active participant in its own defense.

      h2 The Death of the Firewall
      p Traditional firewalls were designed for a world where we knew exactly where the boundaries were. In today's serverless and edge-computed world, there are no boundaries. We need something more agile, more "claw-like" that can latch onto threats at the very edge.

      h2 Resilience Over Prevention
      p We've spent decades trying to prevent breaches. The Claw model assumes breaches will happen and focuses on absolute resilience — the ability to compartmentalize and heal automatically.
